        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(x-1)(1+x+x^2+\\cdots+x^{n-1})=x^n-1$.\n\nExpand the right-hand side; the intervening powers cancel.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x-1)(1+x+x^2+\\cdots+x^{n-1})&=(x+x^2+\\cdots+x^n)-(1+x+x^2+\\cdots+x^{n-1})\\\\(x-1)(1+x+x^2+\\cdots+x^{n-1})&=x^n-1.\\end{align*}$$\nEvery term from $x$ to $x^{n-1}$ cancels.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p12-q97-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, simplify $1+2+2^2+\\cdots+2^{49}$, leaving your answer in index form.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2^{50}-1$.\n\nUse part (a) with $x=2$ and $n=50$.",
          "worked": "Use part (a) with $x=2$ and $n=50$:\n$$2^{50}-1=(2-1)(1+2+2^2+\\cdots+2^{49}).$$\nSince $2-1=1$,\n$$1+2+2^2+\\cdots+2^{49}=2^{50}-1.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
